Support musl in the SwiftGlibc module

The SwiftGlibc umbrella header includes the libc headers with no
feature-test macros, relying on glibc's defaults to expose
__sighandler_t, __environ and lgammal_r, which the Glibc overlay
(Platform.swift, tgmath.swift.gyb) references unconditionally on Linux.
musl declares its GNU extensions (sighandler_t, lgammal_r, ...) only
under _GNU_SOURCE and has no declaration for the other two spellings at
all, although the __environ symbol itself is real on musl (environ is
its weak alias).

Define _GNU_SOURCE and provide the missing glibc spellings when
compiling against musl, keyed off __GLIBC__ from features.h so glibc
builds are completely unaffected.

--- a/stdlib/public/Platform/SwiftGlibc.h.gyb
+++ b/stdlib/public/Platform/SwiftGlibc.h.gyb
@@ -104,6 +104,20 @@
 ]
 }%
 
+/* musl exposes its GNU extensions (sighandler_t, lgammal_r, ...) only under
+ * _GNU_SOURCE, and spells some declarations differently from glibc. Pull in
+ * features.h first so __GLIBC__ is knowable, then paper over the differences
+ * for musl only; glibc sees no change. The __environ symbol is real on musl
+ * (environ is its weak alias), it is merely undeclared. */
+#include <features.h>
+#if defined(__linux__) && !defined(__GLIBC__)
+#ifndef _GNU_SOURCE
+#define _GNU_SOURCE 1
+#endif
+typedef void (*__sighandler_t)(int);
+extern char **__environ;
+#endif
+
 % for header in headers:
 #if __has_include(<${header}>)
 #include <${header}>
